<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sasol plans 96 mln rand reformer upgrade.</title>
<headline>Sasol plans 96 mln rand reformer upgrade.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Synthetic fuel producer Sasol Ltd said on Wednesday it planned to convert 16 ignition catalyst reformers to an open-flame type at its Secunda plant, at a cost of 96 million rand.</p>
<p>The conversion will take place between February and October next year.</p>
<p>Sasol said the new system should increase efficiency and extend the life of the catalyst, effectively meaning that the periods between shutdowns for replacement of catalyst will be longer than before.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
